      "text": "tempter came … command that these stones be made bread, Matt. 4:3. Give us this day our daily bread, Matt. 6:11. if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone, Matt. 7:9. he took the seven loaves and the fishes, Matt. 15:36. disciples … had forgotten to take bread, Matt. 16:5 (Mark 8:14). Jesus took bread … this is my body, Matt. 26:26 (Mark 14:22; Luke 22:19; 1 Cor. 11:23). they should take … no scrip, no bread, Mark 6:8 (Luke 9:3). Blessed is he that shall eat bread in the kingdom, Luke 14:15. Whence shall we buy bread, John 6:5. my Father giveth you the true bread, John 6:32. Jesus then cometh, and taketh bread, John 21:13. continued steadfastly … in breaking of bread, Acts 2:42. disciples came together to break bread, Acts 20:7. bread which we break, is it not the communion, 1 Cor. 10:16. as often as ye eat this bread, 1 Cor. 11:26. they work, and eat their own bread, 2 Thes. 3:12.",
